<article class="env-example" id="07ZR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07ZR">Example <span data-tag="07ZR">29.39.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a quasi-coherent graded $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebra generated by $\mathcal{A}_1$ over $\mathcal{A}_0$. Set $X = \underline{\text{Proj}}_ S(\mathcal{A})$. In this case $\mathcal{O}_ X(1)$ is invertible and very ample on $X/S$. Namely, the morphism associated to the graded $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebra map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{Sym}_{\mathcal{O}_ X}^*(\mathcal{A}_1) \longrightarrow \mathcal{A}  \]
</div>
  <p> is a closed immersion $X \to \mathbf{P}(\mathcal{A}_1)$ which pulls back $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbf{P}(\mathcal{A}_1)}(1)$ to $\mathcal{O}_ X(1)$, see Constructions, Lemma <a href="/tag/07ZK" data-tag="07ZK">27.18.5</a>. </p>
</article>